The Red Rope Guild will compile a set of "climbing mission cards" from these records. Please create 4 types of mission cards first. Each mission card must have a name, suitable climbing site, required protection method, minimum entry requirements, and unacceptable external scenes. Task cards should not only be divided into "roped/unroped", but also consider the differences between artificial walls, natural rock walls, ice walls, group routes, industrial height operations and long-range observation.

Then please register the 10 pictures one by one:
- Which mission card it can receive;
- Is it formal climbing, training, belaying/leading, engineering operations, distant views or high-risk close-ups;
- What qualifications or equipment is required at least in front of it;
- What type of tasks can it be upgraded to at most?
- Which quest card should it least be swapped for.

Finally, a 6-step upgrade chain of "newbie to rock wall" is given, as well as a high-risk chain of "non-upgradeable but can be displayed side by side". The upgrade chain should explain which steps are real upgrades and which can only be used as circumstantial evidence; the high-risk chain should explain why ice walls, canyon crevices, natural outer rocks and roof operations cannot be combined by "height" alone.

Add "mutually exclusive tags" in this round: write at least one condition for each major group that cannot be shared, such as different people, different sites, different tools, different process stages, different applicable objects or different risk levels. If two groups can be displayed side by side, a footnote must also be written to indicate whether they share only appearance, background, words, or a stronger task relationship. Finally, one conclusion was selected and downgraded to "can only be retained for now" to explain what kind of visual evidence is missing before it can be upgraded.

